 "notes": "Reqqa Point on Gozo's north coast: the entry at the point, the chimney near it, Reqqa reef running north-west under water to 15–17 m, the wall beyond it to 60 m and more with the Bottleneck shaft (58 to 35 m), and Billinghurst Cave in the bay to the west. Coastline, the entry and Billinghurst Cave are from OpenStreetMap; the layout follows the St Andrew's Divers Cove (gozodive.com) description and maltadives.com site coordinates. The reef, sand and wall outlines are estimated, not surveyed, so all positions are approximate.",
